<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Hammu Musa II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1323">1323</a>–<a href="/years/1389">1389</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Hammu Musa II was sultan of the Zayyanid Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a> from 1359 to 1389. He restored the dynasty after a period of Marinid occupation and spent much of his reign fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinids</a> and rebellious Arab tribes. A poet and patron of scholars, he wrote a manual of advice on kingship for his son Abu Tashfin, who later rebelled against him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abu-hammu-musa-ii.jpg" alt="Abu Hammu Musa II" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stephen Album Rare Coins · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zayyanid_Dinar_-_Abu_Hammu_II_(1359-1389).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
